The packages under alsa, asp, audio, aec, beat, denoise, echoref, fft, hook, i2c,
mwwfront, oww, rate, safe, safename, spectrum, subband, tflite, unseen, vec,
and the microphone and the speaker under mic and speaker, are TECHO5's,
copied with only the import paths rewritten, the licence noted above, and
the framework's own configuration, board description and service plumbing
replaced by the shim under mic/framework. The wake word engine under
third_party/microwakeword is TECHO5's too, with its import paths
rewritten.

The shim under mic/framework stands in for the parts of TECHO5's daemon
framework that the audio code used: the configuration, the board the build
is for, and the software mute. The audio code reads them where it expects
them, so that the audio code itself stays as it was written and as it was
tested.

TECHO5's own tests came with the code, and they run here unchanged.

